//@ compile-fail
//@ error-pattern: error[E040]: Sounio uses 'var' instead of 'let mut'
// E040: Rust `let mut` is rejected with a helpful diagnostic (use `var`).
// The pattern names the tag AND the text. A bare `E040` matched vacuously:
// the harness greps the whole compile output case-insensitively, and the
// compiler echoes `source: tests/compile-fail/rust_let_mut_e040.sio` -- so
// this fixture passed on its own FILENAME, before and after lean_single
// learned to print the number. Keyed like this it fails on an engine that
// prints the message untagged, which is what it is here to assert.
fn main() -> i32 with IO {
    let mut x = 0
    x as i32
}
